    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000023
    m_Localized: "Madame Quacking!\nI scarce know how to express my deep obligation
      for receiving me. As a gentleman of rational mind, I clung until this very
      hour to the hope that I might avoid\u2026 these occult superfluities. Pray,
      madam, look into the past and tell me\u2014who was the villain that murdered
      my wife?"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000024
    m_Localized: "It was a gloomy, overcast evening. Mrs. Foxington and I set forth
      in the carriage towards the estate of Sir Oswald Blackmore \u2014 the wealthiest
      badger in all the kingdom. He was hosting a charitable supper, at which Miss
      Foxington was to perform."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000025
    m_Localized: 'The reception was splendid, with a great many guests.

      Yet
      in the first part of the evening, Miss Foxington and I were parted. As the
      celebrated pianist, she was much approached by admirers.

      I, meanwhile,
      met Lady Bella Nottingham, and we became quite absorbed in reminiscences.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000026
    m_Localized: 'When the guests had wearied of talk, Sir Oswald Blackmore rose
      and gave a short, rather empty speech on the virtues of patronage.

      Then
      Miss Foxington took the floor: a stately polonaise and several familiar nocturnes
      followed; the company applauded warmly.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000027
    m_Localized: 'Miss Foxington was soon surrounded by an admiring circle of guests,
      while I gave myself over to a growing ennui.

      I daresay I had indulged
      rather too freely in the wine, for I failed altogether to mark the moment when
      she slipped away.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000028
    m_Localized: I know not how much time had passed, but presently Sir Oswald Blackmore
      proposed that we stroll into the winter garden and smoke a cigar apiece. My
      head was ringing from the wine I had taken, yet Blackmore spoke readily and
      required no reply from me.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000029
    m_Localized: 'This horror is beyond words! The drunken fog vanished the instant
      I saw her lying on the wet ground. Her gown was soiled, her fur matted, her
      eyes fixed and lifeless.

      How - how am I to live with this now?'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000030
    m_Localized: 
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000031
    m_Localized: "Doctor Nicholas Moorley and Madame Foxington rode in the carriage
      towards the estate of Sir Oswald Blackmore \u2014 the wealthiest badger in
      all the kingdom"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000032
    m_Localized: 'The grand reception at the estate was in full splendour.

      Doctor
      Moorley met his old acquaintance, Lady Bella Nottingham, and they soon fell
      into reminiscences.

      Sir Oswald Blackmore then presented the young romantic
      poet Theodore Lapwood to the guests.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000033
    m_Localized: Madame Foxington played a solemn polonaise and several well-known
      nocturnes. The guests were captivated.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000034
    m_Localized: 'Doctor Moorley retired to a quiet corner, there to drown his thoughts
      in wine.

      Madame Foxington excused herself and vanished from the assembly.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000035
    m_Localized: Doctor Moorley and Sir Oswald Blackmore strolled together through
      the winter garden.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000036
    m_Localized: All the guests now stood gathered in the winter garden, frozen in
      horrified silence over the lifeless form of Madame Foxington.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
